==Point system==
Players final position on each map are added to calculate total points as per below:
# <b>5</b> points
# <b>4</b> points
# <b>3</b> points
# <b>2</b> points
# <b>2</b> points
# <b>1</b> point
# <b>1</b> point
# <b>1</b> point (only in grand final)
# <b>1</b> point (only in grand final)
<br>
If players are tied on a map, those players will receive the same amount of points from that map.

==== Tiebreakers ====
If the players are tied in the table on points, the tiebreaker will be:
# The highest spot a player managed to be on a map (a 1st place beats a 2nd place etc).
# If still tied, both/all players advance to the Grand Final.
# Frags. If there are too many players tied - that advance to the Grand Final - total frags on all maps will decide. 
# If players are still tied and there are too many players who advance to the Grand Final, we will need another qualifier of 2 groups.
<br>
If players are tied after 6 maps in the grand final, they will split the money with equal shares. They need to be tied on points and placements (the more higher map placements wins).

